          #AtiyahGroupoidIsCechNerve.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              By the discussion at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-image"} 1-image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              in an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              is equivalently given as the canonical map given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi im
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Y
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \to im_1(f) \simeq \underset{\rightarrow}{\lim} (X^{\times^{\bullet+1}_Y})
                    \\,.
            %p
              This means that regarded as an object of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grpd(\mathbf{H})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi At
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} At(P)
              %em is
              simply the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
              of the classifying map. This means that the definition of Atiyah groupoids in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
              is much more fundamental than in traditional
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#equivalence_of_atiyahgroupoid_bisections_to_slice_automorphisms Equivalence of Atiyah-groupoid bisections to slice automorphisms
          %p
            We discuss how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+of+bisections"} ∞-group of bisections
            of a higher Atiyah groupoid is canonically equivalent to the
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
            of the modulating map that gave rise to it, regarded as an object in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
            over its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
          %p To this end we need the following two definitions
          #HValuedAutomorphismGroup.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              in an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
