            regarded as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+bundle"} prequantum bundle
          %p (…)
          %h3#TheQuantomorphismNGroups
            The quantomorphism
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#Rogers"}> Rogers 11
            ) is a proposal for the generalization of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            to a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+n-algebra"} Poisson Lie n-algebra
            induced by an
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-plectic+manifold"} n-plectic manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            is traditionally known as the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+group"} quantomorphism group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+n-algebras"} Poisson Lie n-algebras
            should be called an
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+n-group"} quantomorphism n-group
          %p
            We here discuss a general abstract theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+n-groups"} quantomorphism n-groups
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groups+of+bisections"} ∞-groups of bisections
            of a higher Atiyah groupoid associated with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-connections"} principal ∞-connections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+differentiation"} Lie differentiation
            this reproduces the construction in (
            %a{:href => "#Rogers11"}> Rogers 11
            ).
