          %h2#references References
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "#TheTraditionalCourantLie2Algebroid"} above
            identification of higher Atiyah groupoids of “bundle gerbes with connective structure but without
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curving"} curving
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integrating
            the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Courant+Lie+2-algebroid"} standard Courant Lie 2-algebroid
            is directly implied (under the above translations) by the main result in
          %ul
            %li#Collier
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Braxton+Collier"}> Braxton Collier
              ,
              %em Infinitesimal Symmetries of Dixmier-Douady Gerbes
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1108.1525"}> arXiv:1108.1525
              )
          %p
            The corresponding inclusion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+2-algebra"} Poisson Lie 2-algebra
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra"} Lie 2-algebra
            of bisections of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant+Lie+2-algebroid"} Courant Lie 2-algebroid
            was first observed in
          %ul
            %li#Rogers10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
              ,
              %em 2-plectic geometry, Courant algebroids, and categorified prequantization
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1009.2975"} arXiv:1009.2975
          %p
            in the context of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-plectic+geometry"} 2-plectic geometry
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+n-algebra"} Poisson Lie n-algebra
            over an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-plectic+manifold"} n-plectic manifold
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#spring"}
